[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-125719"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/8ba69d7bfe8dd363288bbf86661172004b21143f02c70260da0c184f066a7c12.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y)=⟨{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3},\\,y{e}^{y+1}+x⟩,$ which of the following is equivalent to ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite our integral as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3})\\,dx+(y{e}^{y+1}+x)\\,dy.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/3b90abecc774b5ba5dcee19385fef38b14206d2c31c3b6cba38216bfa9957448.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3}$ and $Q(x,y)=y{e}^{y+1}+x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{3})\\,dx-(y{e}^{y+1}+x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(1-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(1-3\\cdot {r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-3{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686/selection/b7f3ca9ba705e23d2376101eab8dc4019b8e88eb278ff38b17d2895ff3772b11" :answer/id #uuid "229a0908-ea5e-5643-9b41-5b5742e54e00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686/selection/62e396052e696ba8635fd7954f5845fe014e5c9b7c62b03d5b73a97840214280" :answer/id #uuid "d6115739-19d5-52c3-84c7-d2e689185b43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686/selection/7884ba79b265ac8fbe20e5c4e17e76d276c7ffeb70a1a6e7440a575002ba62de" :answer/id #uuid "9980c91b-cb47-5f99-9c24-10cd17ba48e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686/selection/c6d409ee948b7bfbf4eea6f54c1422ffb7c003bcf46f24037411318370977356" :answer/id #uuid "dfd08c1d-7fcb-5467-8ecf-dc4116090e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686/selection/26e3789e4a8d30d9f6da07ffa6f8ce84bb4aee745bed63850b4e9e1d92389c65" :answer/id #uuid "daab7196-75ee-5175-81bb-5018c5a64555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "40a04b29-f889-5a24-a38e-1159cf6cd53d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126686/selection/c6d409ee948b7bfbf4eea6f54c1422ffb7c003bcf46f24037411318370977356" :answer-field/choices ["q-126686/selection/b7f3ca9ba705e23d2376101eab8dc4019b8e88eb278ff38b17d2895ff3772b11" "q-126686/selection/62e396052e696ba8635fd7954f5845fe014e5c9b7c62b03d5b73a97840214280" "q-126686/selection/7884ba79b265ac8fbe20e5c4e17e76d276c7ffeb70a1a6e7440a575002ba62de" "q-126686/selection/c6d409ee948b7bfbf4eea6f54c1422ffb7c003bcf46f24037411318370977356" "q-126686/selection/26e3789e4a8d30d9f6da07ffa6f8ce84bb4aee745bed63850b4e9e1d92389c65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126686" :question/id #uuid "b97bdd87-b8e7-5fa0-84d3-dcb91e945069" :question/math-academy-id "q-126686" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/e44543ad51864a7db6b8e80b5c560a1ac773a7537573014f737451af4d1209a7.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dy\\,?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/d8ee02b2b7282349604dc6305c0b2be796cfdbd2937e06d089e660683a5785ad.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(x{y}^{2}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(2xy-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 5,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{5}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126686/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5704a2-acbe-5ccb-98dc-aa77e0ccd803"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687/selection/bf118cc6de60df7d4597ac631a1e309ddeb0471e88d7b250670424f8e6dadf1a" :answer/id #uuid "aa6ac347-f7e3-5f27-925b-11f80acce604" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687/selection/7c696d7b543e372312718caed2e7da2cc89d1a240b45e2e1d5edb7cf90d06e3a" :answer/id #uuid "c18ce837-d0d2-5ba2-8bdf-67e133e2fb1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}2{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687/selection/6d3153123a843f42ac406044a7bb2a7c59ab1c71b910b47892822f49e89cf64f" :answer/id #uuid "b13f0e98-1625-5fc5-9463-5ed239808695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}3{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687/selection/ed33dcd978381b88bb02a6e004fcc3f46d185d7f11b8d3944101534ab15bb922" :answer/id #uuid "a6036a58-5415-507a-b060-5e0fcdbaf879" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}r(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687/selection/738dc0431f021b1c20b91f9aab960cfa3803aeb5302351b787714069692f2bcc" :answer/id #uuid "11b922f4-d37a-5953-933c-664e05647d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90afa4b1-b9f6-514b-a164-257986be804d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126687/selection/6d3153123a843f42ac406044a7bb2a7c59ab1c71b910b47892822f49e89cf64f" :answer-field/choices ["q-126687/selection/bf118cc6de60df7d4597ac631a1e309ddeb0471e88d7b250670424f8e6dadf1a" "q-126687/selection/7c696d7b543e372312718caed2e7da2cc89d1a240b45e2e1d5edb7cf90d06e3a" "q-126687/selection/6d3153123a843f42ac406044a7bb2a7c59ab1c71b910b47892822f49e89cf64f" "q-126687/selection/ed33dcd978381b88bb02a6e004fcc3f46d185d7f11b8d3944101534ab15bb922" "q-126687/selection/738dc0431f021b1c20b91f9aab960cfa3803aeb5302351b787714069692f2bcc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126687" :question/id #uuid "208a1083-56ad-5853-aae0-e9bfc216a1b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-126687" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/e49bde14ba6097dfc7b153d5b93c2be2462b141a37357bfff826c852fc1136eb.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}(2-xy+2{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+xy)\\,dy\\,?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/8b3c794f11c0a9be558e66c1c7a4ae4cd996037bbd6e491eefaa1a2e9000c596.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=2-xy+2{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+xy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-x+4y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(2-xy+2{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+xy)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+y-(-x+4y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3x-3y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 8,\\,-\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(3x-3y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}3{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126687/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e5704a2-acbe-5ccb-98dc-aa77e0ccd803"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756/selection/e779e901de5d03536d19f2efa585c8a793dffe462ce3c2e69b4b3818930753b0" :answer/id #uuid "eb82bb64-7e72-5ce3-bd7e-f0f588aef175" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{81\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756/selection/5f5f9953f5ccca4eea42ef41abc5df7393f4da8e15e36df49e0c0cfdc4a94d5f" :answer/id #uuid "80522476-fae7-5579-8543-aeb55dcd8c5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756/selection/5eaa9664236f2cbe0493a21ae883a528dc1367869c5f227579e48794e91f3d41" :answer/id #uuid "92045d9d-3bfd-5000-a8a4-1ebec6775423" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "56f8af69-44dc-5e3f-a4ae-eb66ec35dc80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756/selection/7073ddf865f0c9f97383f3a07b5458c92de9192b8b4e23bd69709c0792828aba" :answer/id #uuid "645ddde7-ebed-59a9-9543-6eac390d38aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "093ca155-1c15-5460-a43a-aabbb97c8b18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126756/selection/e779e901de5d03536d19f2efa585c8a793dffe462ce3c2e69b4b3818930753b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-126756/selection/e779e901de5d03536d19f2efa585c8a793dffe462ce3c2e69b4b3818930753b0" "q-126756/selection/5f5f9953f5ccca4eea42ef41abc5df7393f4da8e15e36df49e0c0cfdc4a94d5f" "q-126756/selection/5eaa9664236f2cbe0493a21ae883a528dc1367869c5f227579e48794e91f3d41" "q-126756/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-126756/selection/7073ddf865f0c9f97383f3a07b5458c92de9192b8b4e23bd69709c0792828aba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126756" :question/id #uuid "44f0dbe7-0e3a-5de7-ab4d-8d28f09f8e89" :question/math-academy-id "q-126756" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/d675e8d06f2037531a2eec3a7e48374bb0d2e5cb59adfee0cbee5ce3a23add67.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where the path $C$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/96998e4a17d20459622486970518a677309b23fd936c993d8c97dcf0d65a9a29.png)\n\n \n\nNow, since \n\n$$\nP(x,y)={e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y,\\,Q(x,y)={e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2},\n$$\n\n we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{y}+2x{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2{y}^{2}-(-2{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate our double integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2({r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{r}^{3}({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\frac{81}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}[\\theta ]_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-126756/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2eca638-7c7b-51ed-99e3-3b3156d13669"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758/selection/312bfa770061935528fdd11247e1f364b9e5d083ce435303a5ae89b5bbb03a2f" :answer/id #uuid "9879f38c-33ca-5de8-8de2-56c97bbc7e10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{90\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758/selection/e53dac272c2900e538760a4b9a7af88fe393e47303b3643d739d457de50d183c" :answer/id #uuid "00d2476b-0d02-5aca-ba27-7774ad2faa1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758/selection/de3b57990fd61700b99eafb6e691b45557fcf22ee2c12d575512e46ba821430d" :answer/id #uuid "100f768c-bec2-56ed-8832-0cb281284a24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{45\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758/selection/48c2d84e9f8df4acb4d81305febc8e970c68a5a7e3b4c095f0477013aaae36eb" :answer/id #uuid "ff94dc02-10ca-5e75-a954-d2579ea25d0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758/selection/b14cd9a1383b83830b64f7e8a36b4fafc3772da8cffb250acf7a73d317d27992" :answer/id #uuid "2207c320-7528-51ca-badd-e1635a1c99fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3835ccf8-f8a6-5e2c-bc0d-83549731713d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126758/selection/b14cd9a1383b83830b64f7e8a36b4fafc3772da8cffb250acf7a73d317d27992" :answer-field/choices ["q-126758/selection/312bfa770061935528fdd11247e1f364b9e5d083ce435303a5ae89b5bbb03a2f" "q-126758/selection/e53dac272c2900e538760a4b9a7af88fe393e47303b3643d739d457de50d183c" "q-126758/selection/de3b57990fd61700b99eafb6e691b45557fcf22ee2c12d575512e46ba821430d" "q-126758/selection/48c2d84e9f8df4acb4d81305febc8e970c68a5a7e3b4c095f0477013aaae36eb" "q-126758/selection/b14cd9a1383b83830b64f7e8a36b4fafc3772da8cffb250acf7a73d317d27992"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126758" :question/id #uuid "885d7e93-ddfe-5056-8a1a-3e87c6540035" :question/math-academy-id "q-126758" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/bcdc0f59fa284c2b1f1621e7de057ef6f0e084d2eca6732fbc5eae3f74ede113.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∮}_{C}(\\sqrt{5+x}-3{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{-{y}^{2}}+3x{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where the path $C$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070891/assets/6273034b38059d3d49b2a29c91052c290151b4a29073f1c925172dd1c4c2bf72.png)\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\sqrt{5+x}-3{x}^{2}y,\\,Q(x,y)={e}^{-{y}^{2}}+3x{y}^{2},\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-3{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(\\sqrt{5+x}-3{x}^{2}y)dx+({e}^{-{y}^{2}}+x{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3{y}^{2}-(-3{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate our double integral, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}3({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}3{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}60\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =180[\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =180\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =90\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-126758/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2eca638-7c7b-51ed-99e3-3b3156d13669"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126758"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
